{
  "id": "pipes_and_tubes___temperature_expansion",
  "title": "Pipes and Tubes - Temperature Expansion",
  "description": "Calculate the temperature-induced expansion of pipes based on the linear expansion coefficient, pipe length, and temperature difference using the formula: dl = α × Lo × dt",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Pipe Temperature Expansion Calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "pipe_length",
          "label": "Pipe Length (Lo)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "ft"
        },
        {
          "id": "initial_temp",
          "label": "Initial Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 32,
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "final_temp",
          "label": "Final Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 212,
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "expansion_coeff",
          "label": "Linear Expansion Coefficient (α)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.000008,
          "unit": "in/in°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "length_unit",
          "label": "Length Unit",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "feet",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "feet",
              "label": "Feet"
            },
            {
              "value": "inches",
              "label": "Inches"
            },
            {
              "value": "meters",
              "label": "Meters"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "temp_difference",
          "label": "Temperature Difference (dt)",
          "formula": "inputs.final_temp - inputs.initial_temp",
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "pipe_length_inches",
          "label": "Pipe Length in Inches",
          "formula": "inputs.length_unit === 'feet' ? inputs.pipe_length * 12 : inputs.length_unit === 'meters' ? inputs.pipe_length * 39.37 : inputs.pipe_length",
          "unit": "inches"
        },
        {
          "id": "expansion",
          "label": "Thermal Expansion (dl)",
          "formula": "inputs.expansion_coeff * inputs.pipe_length * 12 * (inputs.final_temp - inputs.initial_temp)",
          "unit": "inches",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Material",
        "32-212°F",
        "32-400°F",
        "32-600°F",
        "32-750°F",
        "32-900°F",
        "32-1100°F",
        "32-1300°F"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Alloy Steel (1% Cr, 1/2% Mo)",
          8,
          8.4,
          8.8,
          9.2,
          9.6,
          9.8,
          null
        ],
        [
          "Mild Steel (0.1-0.2% C)",
          7.8,
          8.3,
          8.7,
          9,
          9.5,
          9.7,
          null
        ],
        [
          "Stainless Steel (18% Cr, 8% Ni)",
          11.1,
          11.5,
          11.8,
          12.1,
          12.4,
          12.6,
          12.8
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Thermal Expansion Formula\n\n**dl = α × Lo × dt**\n\nWhere:\n- **dl** = expansion (m, inches)\n- **Lo** = length of pipe (m, inches)\n- **dt** = temperature difference (°C, °F)\n- **α** = linear expansion coefficient (m/m°K, in/in°F)\n\n### Example\nAn alloy steel pipe with length 100 feet is heated from 32 to 212°F. The expansion coefficient is 8×10⁻⁶ (in/in°F).\n\n**Calculation:**\ndl = (8×10⁻⁶ in/in°F) × (100 ft × 12 in/ft) × (212°F - 32°F) = **1.728 inches**"
    }
  ]
}